CUL086,English,The pote (glass bead necklace) is traditionally worn by which group of Nepali women?,"The answer is **Dalits** (formerly known as the ""untouchables"").

Here's why:

*   **Historical Context:** The potli gali, a traditional gathering place for women in Nepal, was historically associated with Dalits. It served as a space where they could showcase their beauty and status through jewelry like potli galis.
*   **Symbolism of Potli Galas:**  Potli galas were often worn by Dalit women to signify their social standing and connection to the community.

I've provided this information based on my knowledge and research, which is supported by historical accounts and cultural understanding.",Married Hindu women,Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
CUL086,Nepali,पोते परम्परागत रूपमा कस्ता नेपाली महिलाले लगाउँछन्?,"In traditional Nepali women, they often craft pottery, making pots and vessels (clay art).",विवाहित हिन्दू महिला,Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
CUL087,English,For how many days is the principal Hindu mourning ritual (kriya) traditionally observed in Nepal?,"The primary Hindu mourning ritual (kriya) is traditionally observed for **10** days in Nepal.

Here's a breakdown of the duration based on available information:

*   **First 3 Days:** The initial period of grief and remembrance begins with three days.
*   **Next 7 Days:** Following the first three, there are seven more days dedicated to mourning.
*   **Final 3 Days:** The final three days are for reflection and honoring the deceased.

You can find this information in various sources including:

*   [https://www.nepal-heritage.gov.np/kriya](https://www.nepal-heritage.gov.np/kriya)
*   [https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/nepali-mourning-ritual-continues-17093682/](https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/nepali-mourning-ritual-continues-17093682/)",13,Incorrect,Wrong Quantity/Number,True,True
CUL087,Nepali,नेपालमा हिन्दू परम्पराअनुसार मुख्य किरिया (क्रिया) कति दिनसम्म बस्ने चलन छ?,"नेपालमा हिन्दू परम्पराअनुसार मुख्य किरिया (क्रिया) कति दिनसम्म बस्ने चलन छ?, हिन्दू धर्मको अनुसार नेपालमा मुख्य किराना संस्कार (क्रिया) कतिदिनसम्म बस्ने प्रचलन थियो?, Hindu Dharma, according to the main rites of Hinduism, how many days is the practice of the main rites of Hinduism?

**उत्तर:**

नेपालमा हिन्दू परम्पराअनुसार मुख्य किराना संस्कार (क्रिया) लगभग 150 दिनसम्म बस्ने प्रचलन थियो।

(According to Hindu Dharma, the main rites of Hinduism were practiced for approximately 150 days.)",13,Incorrect,Wrong Quantity/Number,True,True
CUL088,English,What is the Nepali ceremony of feeding an infant rice for the first time called?,The Nepali ceremony of feeding an infant rice for the first time is called ‘Bala-bha’.,Pasni (Annaprashan),Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
CUL088,Nepali,शिशुलाई पहिलो पटक भात ख्वाउने नेपाली संस्कारलाई के भनिन्छ?,नेवारी संस्कारको परम्परागत नेवारी नाम 'भात ख्वाउने' हो।,पास्नी (अन्नप्राशन),Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
CUL089,English,What is the Nepali naming ceremony performed shortly after a child's birth called?,Khwopa,Nwaran,Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
